+.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-scripts/verdict-cures-round20.txt:6:Concrete failure: interruption while `shasum` writes directly to `MANIFEST-ga.sha256` can leave a valid partial manifest after `RUNNER-OVERALL: rc=0` was recorded. On rerun, `validate_ga_evidence` checks only the listed hashes; it does not require exactly the expected 11 basenames. It reuses and commits the partial evidence, and the delta guard rejects only after the verdict commit, leaving a non-rerunnable state.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-ga/transcript-ga-2.log:17728: trailing whitespace.
+.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-scripts/verdict-cures-round20.txt:10:Concrete failure: `MONITOR_ONLY=1` does not prevent the evidence runner and commit-1 phase. After a post-tag monitoring timeout, an accidental local truncation of an evidence file makes validation rerun Codex and commit new evidence, moving HEAD beyond the already-pushed tag. The script then skips verdict/CI/tag creation, monitors the old tag, and declares GA with an untagged, unpushed local HEAD—the subsequent W3 instructions anchor the wrong commit.  
