   140	    # install legs + 1 upgrade leg PER ceremony mode, and the positive control
   141	    # runs the same again with a planted divergence: 12 install/upgrade
   142	    # operations added to this job. Local wall time (Darwin arm64, 16 cores,
   143	    # 2026-08-05): gate 122s + control 118s = 240s. A 2-core ubuntu-latest
   144	    # runner is the usual 2-3x slower, i.e. 8-12 min of NEW work on top of the
   145	    # ~5 min this job already spent. 15 would sit inside the noise band, and
   146	    # the perf-gate N=20 flake (PLAN-159) was exactly that mistake. Re-tighten
   147	    # once real CI runs give a p95.
   148	    # PLAN-166 F3 (assembler): 20 -> 25. The spec-ownership e2e adds 4 more
   149	    # installs + 3 upgrades (S1-S8; ~3-4 min local per the W1-C measurement),
   150	    # i.e. up to ~8-10 more CI minutes at the same 2-3x factor. Same
   151	    # anti-flake sizing rule as the F4 bump above.
   152	    # PLAN-177 W1 (CF-9): 25 -> 32. The night-mode efficacy e2e adds 3 installs
   153	    # + 2 upgrades. MEASURED, not guessed: 2m06s wall on Darwin arm64 (16
   154	    # cores, 2026-08-13), reproduced across two runs. At the same 2-3x runner
   155	    # factor this workflow already sizes with, that is 4-7 CI minutes, so +7.
   156	    # A job-level timeout that clips a green run reports as `cancelled` on an
   157	    # innocent step (the S2xx lesson), so the margin stays deliberate.
