   168	      # PLAN-166 F4: the parity e2e's historical leg installs from a PINNED
   169	      # TAG. `fetch-depth: 1` produces a checkout with NO tags, so the pin
   170	      # would not resolve and the gate would die before comparing a single
   171	      # tree - "it passes on my clone" is precisely the hole this test exists
   172	      # to close. The pin is READ FROM THE TEST (--print-pin) so the workflow
   173	      # never becomes a second copy of that truth.
